    "final_cot": "Image description: The figure shows a pentagon, with vertices in order along the boundary as A, B, C, D, E. There are right-angle marks at points A and B, so ∠A = 90°, ∠B = 90°. The figure also marks ∠E = (2x + 10)°, ∠D = x°, ∠C = (2x - 20)°. The problem asks to find m∠C. Reasoning: The sum of the interior angles of a pentagon is (5 - 2) × 180° = 540°. Therefore 90 + 90 + (2x + 10) + x + (2x - 20) = 540. Combining like terms gives 5x + 170 = 540, so 5x = 370, x = 74. Thus m∠C = 2x - 20 = 2(74) - 20 = 148 - 20 = 128°.",
